Which implementations create a thread-safe Singleton? (Select all that apply)

```java
// A: Eager
class SingletonA {
    private static final SingletonA INST = new SingletonA();
    private SingletonA() {}
    public static SingletonA get() { return INST; }
}
// B: Double-Checked Locking
class SingletonB {
    private static volatile SingletonB inst;
    private SingletonB() {}
    public static SingletonB get() {
        if (inst == null) synchronized(SingletonB.class) {
            if (inst == null) inst = new SingletonB();
        }
        return inst;
    }
}
// C: Enum
enum SingletonC { INSTANCE; }
// D: No sync
class SingletonD {
    private static SingletonD inst;
    private SingletonD() {}
    public static SingletonD get() {
        if (inst == null) inst = new SingletonD();
        return inst;
    }
}
```

